ies Services Supervisor I CSA02821P DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt CSA Dakota State University is seeking applications a full-time Facilities Services Supervisor I. This position will work an 8 hour shift Monday through Friday with some weekends as needed to help with preparation/clean-up for events on campus. The hours will be 4:00am-12:30pmResponsibilities Include:General cleaning of an academic building.Floor care mainly vacuuming and mopping but could include ... View Details Bookmark Facility Worker CSA02820P DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt CSA Dakota State University is seeking applications for a full-time facility worker. Primary responsibilities include custodial care and minor maintenance at the Community Center.The position will be scheduled Monday through Friday from 10pm to 6:30am. Responsibilities:Floor care will be daily vacuuming, scrubbing and mopping, occasional carpet shampooing and floor waxing.Clean and sanitize restroo... View Details Bookmark Part-Time Facility Worker CSA02669P DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt CSA Dakota State University is seeking applications for a part-time, non-benefit eligible Facility Worker to work Monday – Friday. Preferred hours are 8pm – 12am.Responsibilities:Floor care: sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, but could also include waxing, and shampooing carpets.Clean and sanitize designated areas.Collect and remove trash from building.Wash walls, woodwork, and windows.Remove snow from ... View Details Bookmark Building Maintenance Specialist - HVAC CSA02698P DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt CSA Dakota State University is seeking applications for a full-time Building Maintenance Specialist – HVAC. This position is responsible for maintaining existing plumbing, heating and cooling systems on the facilities and installing new systems according to state code. The position will report to the Assistant Director of Facilities Trades. Responsibilities:Create estimates for new installations of... View Details Bookmark Leadership Giving Officer NFE03148P DSU-Institutional Advancement NFE Dakota State University seeks a passionate relationship builder to serve as its next Leadership Giving Officer. This role is responsible for identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding alumni, parents, and friends of the university capable of making gifts of $5,000 or more, helping to create philanthropic partnerships that fuel the university’s vision and strengthen its future. Require... View Details Bookmark Part-Time Digital Accessibility Specialist CSA02770P DSU-Information Technology Services CSA Dakota State University is seeking a temporary, part-time Digital Accessibility Specialist to support campus-wide accessibility initiatives. This position plays an important role in helping ensure that digital content is accessible to all users while supporting faculty, staff, and students in creating inclusive learning and working environments.Key ResponsibilitiesAssist with training and suppo... View Details Bookmark Vice President for Institutional Advancement NFE03101P DSU-President NFE Dakota State University (DSU) invites applications and nominations for the position of Vice President for Institutional Advancement and President/CEO of the Dakota State University Foundation. Reporting to the Foundation Board of Trustees and serving as a member of the DSU President’s Cabinet, the Vice President provides strategic leadership for the university’s comprehensive advancement progra... View Details Bookmark The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the 